<http://data.silknow.org/event/adb58d5b-fc3c-3882-b069-3c3696bcd96e>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Purchased. Registered File number 1989/1718.\nLeopold Iklé (1838-1922) was a Swiss textile industrialist and collector. We do not have a provenance for the braid before it entered his collection.\n\nHistorical significance: This is a rare survival of such a braid, as its length, decorative quality and the precious metal content could all have made it subject to reuse, or burning to extract the metal (which often happened to metal lace and other textiles containing metal thread)."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8efa4cd5-40a6-3340-8470-0b35ecbdc729> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Purchased. Registered File number 1989/1718.\nLeopold Iklé (1838-1922) was a Swiss textile industrialist and collector. We do not have a provenance for the braid before it entered his collection.\n\nHistorical significance: This is a rare survival of such a braid, as its length, decorative quality and the precious metal content could all have made it subject to reuse, or burning to extract the metal (which often happened to metal lace and other textiles containing metal thread)."@en .

