<http://data.silknow.org/object/8efa4cd5-40a6-3340-8470-0b35ecbdc729/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Girdle of braided silk and metal thread. Length of passementerie, probably intended for a girdle. It is intact with decorative knots weighting it at each end. The two outer elements are of narrow green silk braid with metal thread (gilt strip wound around a white silk core) wound in and out in regular groups of loops. These are joined cross-wise at intervals with short braids of green silk and metal thread, and between them linking them, are open and tight knots of metal thread."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8efa4cd5-40a6-3340-8470-0b35ecbdc729> .

